# Response headers, for Cloudflare Pages (Netlify reads the same file).
#
# Vite names every file it emits under /assets/ by a hash of its content, so a
# name never holds different bytes: a browser may keep one for a year and never
# ask again. Without this rule Pages sends `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`,
# which the zone's Browser Cache TTL raises to four hours, and a returning
# visitor re-checks every script each time. A longer max-age than the Browser
# Cache TTL is passed through as it is. The HTML that names the assets keeps
# Pages' default and is revalidated, so a deploy is picked up at once.
#
# Pages applies this file to what its static asset handler serves: every path
# public/_routes.json does not send to _worker.js, which /assets/* is not.
# deploy/local/Caddyfile sends the same header on the self-hosted image, and
# scripts/release/monitor.py checks it in production.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
